* The Newton interpolant of ` z ^ - ( M + 1 ) ` on the square takes the value ` v_j ^ - ( M + 1 ) ` at the nodes inside and 0 outside, so ` sum_j v_j ^ ( M + 1 ) P ( v_j ) ` counts the inside nodes; the node ` v_J = 1 ` is inside, so the count is at least 1.

